<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    >
    <title><%= h(@name) %>: the archived result</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="The archived result of an election recorded on Bitcoin SV, with the files to recount it offline."
    >
    <style>
      :root {
        --page: #ffffff;
        --inset: #f9fafb;
        --border: #e5e7eb;
        --heading: #111827;
        --text: #374151;
        --secondary: #4b5563;
        --link: #1d4ed8;
        --link-hover: #1e3a8a;
        --beta-bg: #fef3c7;
        --beta-text: #78350f;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--page);
        color: var(--text);
        font: 16px/1.6 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 44rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem;
      }
      h1,
      h2,
      h3 {
        color: var(--heading);
        line-height: 1.25;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 1.875rem;
        margin: 0.5rem 0;
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        margin: 2.25rem 0 0.5rem;
      }
      h3 {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
        margin: 0;
      }
      p,
      li {
        margin: 0.5rem 0;
      }
      a {
        color: var(--link);
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      a:hover {
        color: var(--link-hover);
      }
      .lede {
        color: var(--secondary);
        font-size: 1.125rem;
      }
      .pill {
        display: inline-block;
        border-radius: 9999px;
        background: var(--beta-bg);
        color: var(--beta-text);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        padding: 0.125rem 0.625rem;
      }
      .mono,
      code,
      pre {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      }
      .hash {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }
      code {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        background: var(--inset);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        padding: 0 0.25rem;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }
      pre {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        background: var(--inset);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        white-space: pre-wrap;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }
      pre code {
        background: none;
        border: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }
      ul.cards {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
      }
      .card {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        margin: 0.75rem 0;
      }
      .secondary {
        color: var(--secondary);
        font-size: 0.875rem;
      }
      footer {
        color: var(--secondary);
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        margin-top: 3rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p>
        <span class="pill">Archived result</span>
      </p>
      <h1><%= h(@name) %></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the archived result of an election recorded on Bitcoin SV.
        Every file here is static, so this page works from a folder on your computer or from any web host.
      </p>
      <p>
        The election is <span class="mono hash"><%= h(@election) %></span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        It filled <span class="mono"><%= seats(@number_elected) %></span>, with ballots counted in blocks <span class="mono"><%= @opens_at_height %></span> through <span class="mono"><%= @closes_at_height %></span>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="winners-heading">Winners</h2>
      <%= if @winners == [] do %>
      <p id="winners">
        No candidate received a vote.
      </p>
      <% else %>
      <ol
        id="winners"
        aria-labelledby="winners-heading"
      >
        <%= for name <- @winners do %>
        <li><%= h(name) %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ol>
      <% end %>
      <%= if @undecided do %>
      <p id="undecided">
        <%= seats(@undecided["seats"]) %> undecided, tied between <span class="mono"><%= h(Enum.join(@undecided["tied"], ", ")) %></span>.
      </p>
      <% end %>

      <h2 id="tally-heading">The tally</h2>
      <ul
        id="tally"
        class="cards"
        aria-labelledby="tally-heading"
      >
        <%= for c <- @tally do %>
        <li
          id="candidate-<%= h(c.id) %>"
          class="card"
        >
          <h3><%= h(c.name) %></h3>
          <p class="secondary">
            Id <span class="mono"><%= h(c.id) %></span>
          </p>
          <p>
            <span class="mono"><%= votes(c.votes) %></span><%= if c.elected do %>, elected<% end %>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <span class="mono"><%= @counted %></span> ballots counted, and <span class="mono"><%= @not_counted %></span> not counted.
        <code>count.json</code> lists each one, with the rule a ballot failed.
      </p>

      <h2>The archive and the result record</h2>
      <p>
        The archive's sha256 (<code>archive_sha256</code>) is the sha256 of <a href="MANIFEST.sha256">MANIFEST.sha256</a>, which lists every file of evidence with its own sha256.
      </p>
      <p
        id="archive-sha256"
        class="mono hash"
      ><%= h(@archive_sha256) %></p>
      <%= if @result_txid do %>
      <p id="result-record">
        The result record is transaction <span class="mono hash"><%= h(@result_txid) %></span>.
        It carries the same <code>archive_sha256</code>, signed by the election's administrator.
      </p>
      <% else %>
      <p id="result-record">
        Result record not published yet.
        When it is, it carries this <code>archive_sha256</code>, signed by the election's administrator.
      </p>
      <% end %>
      <%= if @close_block_hash do %>
      <p>
        Block <span class="mono"><%= @closes_at_height %></span>, where voting closed, has the hash <span class="mono hash"><%= h(@close_block_hash) %></span>.
        Check it on any block explorer: it ties these files to the real chain, and it settles a tie for the last seat by lot.
      </p>
      <% end %>

      <h2 id="recount-heading">Recount it yourself</h2>
      <p>
        You don't have to trust this page.
        The recount tool checks every file against the manifest, the blocks against each other, each ballot against its block, and each signature, then counts again with the published rule.
        It makes no network calls.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="recount.html">How to recount, step by step</a></li>
        <li><a href="recount.py">recount.py</a>, the recount tool, one Python 3 file</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        From this folder, in a terminal:
      </p>
      <pre><code>python3 -I recount.py . --archive-sha256 <%= h(@archive_sha256) %></code></pre>
      <%= if @result_txid do %>
      <p>
        Or save the result record's raw transaction as <code>result.hex</code> and check its signature too:
      </p>
      <pre><code>python3 -I recount.py . --result-tx result.hex</code></pre>
      <% end %>
      <p>
        This page, <code>recount.py</code> and <code>recount.html</code> sit beside the manifest, not in it.
        This page shows <code>archive_sha256</code>, so it can't be hashed into the manifest that hash is taken over.
        The tool and guide are copies: compare them with the ones Bitblocks publishes, or read <code>recount.py</code> before you run it.
        What the recount prints, not this page, is the result.
      </p>

      <h2>The files</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="MANIFEST.sha256">MANIFEST.sha256</a>, every file of evidence with its sha256</li>
        <li><a href="archive.json">archive.json</a>, what each file is</li>
        <li><a href="count.json">count.json</a>, the count's input and its result</li>
        <li><a href="roll.json">roll.json</a>, the voter roll, its exact bytes on chain</li>
      </ul>

      <footer>
        <p>
          Bitblocks read the chain and built this archive.
          It did not cast a vote.
          The record format is a draft.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
